    "html": "\n        <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n          <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\n          <span class=\"time\">45 min</span>\n          <span class=\"chip company\">Meta</span><span class=\"chip company\">Amazon</span><span class=\"chip company\">Microsoft</span><span class=\"chip company\">Flipkart</span>\n        </div>\n        <h1>Pattern: Scaling Reads (and Caching Pitfalls)</h1>\n        <p class=\"lead\">Most systems are read far more than they are written. After this page you can climb the read-scaling ladder in an interview - indexes, replicas, caches, CDN, read models - and defend each rung against the failures that interviewers love to poke at: stampedes, hot keys, stale data and cache penetration.</p>\n      "
